#: ../../how-to/fitting/advanced_arima.ipynb:10002
#: 1bae4b6d7c684c12a5c78d07dbb38586
msgid "ARIMA: Time Series Forecasting"
msgstr "ARIMA: 時系列予測"

#: ../../how-to/fitting/advanced_arima.ipynb:10004
#: 22e4ca474ae5437c8eca2a72c56b74ac
msgid ""
"This notebook demonstrates how to model and forecast time series data using "
"ARIMA-related functions (AR, MA, ARMA, ARIMA/SARIMAX) that have been added "
"to the `gwexpy` `TimeSeries` class."
msgstr ""
"このノートブックでは、`gwexpy` の `TimeSeries` クラスに追加された ARIMA 関連の機能（AR, MA, ARMA, "
"ARIMA/SARIMAX）を使用して、時系列データのモデリングと未来予測を行う方法を解説します。"

#: ../../how-to/fitting/advanced_arima.ipynb:10006
#: ../../how-to/fitting/advanced_arima.ipynb:240006
#: 80c1f4c8c8974b74a1f628b8256c4159 9c606b7f17e74707a23676f229457c02
msgid "**Related API**: [Time Series API](../../reference/api/timeseries.rst)"
msgstr "**関連 API**: [Time Series API](../../reference/api/timeseries.rst)"

#: ../../how-to/fitting/advanced_arima.ipynb:10007
#: ../../how-to/fitting/advanced_arima.ipynb:240007
#: 1cad421680044de0a4f239d3a654f47a 5a1625ccacc84bfb89b08f23818c97ea
msgid ""
"**Related theory**: [Validated "
"Algorithms](../../explanation/validated_algorithms.md), [Numerical "
"Stability](../../explanation/numerical_stability.md)"
msgstr ""
"**関連理論**: "
"[検証済みアルゴリズム](../../explanation/validated_algorithms.md)、[数値的安定性](../../explanation/numerical_stability.md)"

#: ../../how-to/fitting/advanced_arima.ipynb:10009
#: 2b78dace5c6b417b85f860d0850ae858
msgid "Setup"
msgstr "準備"

#: ../../how-to/fitting/advanced_arima.ipynb:10011
#: d51260b149b24fbfbdc7fd3c2abe956b
msgid "Import the necessary libraries."
msgstr "必要なライブラリをインポートします。"

#: ../../how-to/fitting/advanced_arima.ipynb:30002
#: cfc2bc6ce4364af9a442faafd029a8c3
msgid "Creating Sample Data"
msgstr "サンプルデータの作成"

#: ../../how-to/fitting/advanced_arima.ipynb:30004
#: bfa9bb222a3a41dbb941ebb4f5bbefdb
msgid ""
"To verify the effectiveness of ARIMA models, we create synthetic data that "
"includes a trend, seasonality (periodicity), and noise."
msgstr "ARIMAモデルの効果を確認するために、トレンド、季節性（周期性）、ノイズを含んだ模擬データを作成します。"

#: ../../how-to/fitting/advanced_arima.ipynb:50002
#: d67725a5a9c2418a8fce13ccdb3da37d
msgid "1. AR (AutoRegressive) Model"
msgstr "1. AR (AutoRegressive) モデル"

#: ../../how-to/fitting/advanced_arima.ipynb:50004
#: e99545a36d6e4b4b983fbfaaa6ffc4c6
msgid ""
"The AR model assumes that the current value depends on past values. Use the "
"`ts.ar(p)` method, where `p` is the order."
msgstr "ARモデルは、現在の値が過去の値に依存すると仮定するモデルです。 `ts.ar(p)` メソッドを使用します。`p` は次数です。"

#: ../../how-to/fitting/advanced_arima.ipynb:70002
#: 56d55aee55354e40a50f904edb3fda1a
msgid "2. MA (Moving Average) Model"
msgstr "2. MA (Moving Average) モデル"

#: ../../how-to/fitting/advanced_arima.ipynb:70004
#: 688dc0aaa23141268985b9bafe71558c
msgid ""
"The MA model assumes that the current value depends on past prediction "
"errors (white noise). Use the `ts.ma(q)` method."
msgstr "MAモデルは、現在の値が過去の予測誤差（ホワイトノイズ）に依存すると仮定するモデルです。 `ts.ma(q)` メソッドを使用します。"

#: ../../how-to/fitting/advanced_arima.ipynb:90002
#: bcb3192ab59f4adeb825b0855ad18b1e
msgid "3. ARMA (AutoRegressive Moving Average) Model"
msgstr "3. ARMA (AutoRegressive Moving Average) モデル"

#: ../../how-to/fitting/advanced_arima.ipynb:90004
#: 0a4e98a926594401bff28b876cc973b8
msgid "The ARMA model combines AR and MA. Use the `ts.arma(p, q)` method."
msgstr "ARとMAを組み合わせたモデルです。 `ts.arma(p, q)` メソッドを使用します。"

#: ../../how-to/fitting/advanced_arima.ipynb:110002
#: 0dd3891c181741529b98b1834c9e82c5
msgid "4. ARIMA / Auto-ARIMA"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/fitting/advanced_arima.ipynb:110004
#: 8fd594aa5dde4730ab1bf29d5f4f7efa
msgid ""
"The ARIMA model removes non-stationarity (such as trends) by differencing, "
"then applies the ARMA model."
msgstr "ARIMAモデルは、差分を取ることで非定常性（トレンドなど）を除去し、ARMAモデルを適用します。"

#: ../../how-to/fitting/advanced_arima.ipynb:110006
#: 067be896f28d40f49f0567bea4407050
msgid ""
"Use the `ts.arima()` method. With the `auto=True` option, the `pmdarima` "
"library is used to automatically search for optimal parameters (p, d, q). "
"This is the most recommended approach."
msgstr ""
"`ts.arima()` メソッドを使用します。 `auto=True` オプションを指定すると、`pmdarima` "
"ライブラリを使用して最適なパラメータ (p, d, q) を自動的に探索します。これが最も推奨される方法です。"

#: ../../how-to/fitting/advanced_arima.ipynb:130002
#: 4001c5074f1940ed9c6ebbbb9978d9ad
msgid "5. Obtaining Forecast Data"
msgstr "5. 予測データの取得"

#: ../../how-to/fitting/advanced_arima.ipynb:130004
#: ee5afc0307c84af08c61899ca276ae07
msgid ""
"Beyond plotting, you can directly obtain forecast values as a `TimeSeries` "
"object using the `.forecast()` method. This also includes confidence "
"intervals."
msgstr ""
"プロットだけでなく、`.forecast()` メソッドを使用して予測値の `TimeSeries` オブジェクトを直接取得できます。 "
"これには信頼区間（Confidence Interval）も含まれます。"

#: ../../how-to/fitting/advanced_arima.ipynb:150002
#: 2ef8c5ee9139424b96fbc6a080823159
msgid ""
"6. Application in Gravitational Wave Data Analysis: Noise Removal "
"(Whitening) with ARIMA"
msgstr "6. 重力波データ解析における応用: ARIMAによるノイズ除去 (Whitening)"

#: ../../how-to/fitting/advanced_arima.ipynb:150004
#: be63d927580746dbbd8435c755c55b84
msgid ""
"In gravitational wave data analysis, a process called **whitening** is "
"performed to extract burst signals or ringdown waveforms from stationary "
"\"colored noise\". By training an ARIMA model as a predictive model for "
"background noise and subtracting the predicted values from the measured "
"values (taking residuals), it is possible to remove noise and enhance the "
"signal."
msgstr ""
"重力波データ解析では、定常的な「有色ノイズ」の中から突発的なバースト信号やリングダウン波形を抽出するために、**白色化 (Whitening)** "
"という処理が行われます。 "
"ARIMAモデルを背景ノイズの予測モデルとして学習させ、実測値からその予測値を引く（残差をとる）ことで、ノイズを除去し信号を強調することが可能です。"

#: ../../how-to/fitting/advanced_arima.ipynb:160002
#: f9bb76dfd3834c95aa9bf26371a28988
msgid "Step 1: Generating Colored Noise and Injecting a Signal"
msgstr "Step 1: 有色ノイズの生成と信号の注入"

#: ../../how-to/fitting/advanced_arima.ipynb:160003
#: bab78e39890a4f129932755293e54499
msgid ""
"First, we create colored noise with strong low-frequency components (AR(1) "
"process), and embed a weak signal (sine-Gaussian) that is difficult to "
"distinguish otherwise. Note: We use \"strain\" as the unit, which is "
"recognizable by Astropy."
msgstr ""
"まず、低周波成分が強い有色ノイズ（AR(1)プロセス）を作成し、そこにそのままでは判別しにくい微弱な信号（サインガウシアン）を埋め込みます。 ※単位には"
" Astropy で認識可能な \"strain\" を使用します。"

#: ../../how-to/fitting/advanced_arima.ipynb:180002
#: 1fd54025dd1b4ee8ad8936080c311f7b
msgid "Step 2: Noise Modeling with ARIMA"
msgstr "Step 2: ARIMAによるノイズモデリング"

#: ../../how-to/fitting/advanced_arima.ipynb:180003
#: 3995fa4466fc4023a81d4835b300e1a9
msgid ""
"Using `auto=True`, we search for the optimal model that expresses the "
"autocorrelation structure of the background noise."
msgstr "`auto=True` を使って、背景ノイズの自己相関構造を表現する最適なモデルを探索します。"

#: ../../how-to/fitting/advanced_arima.ipynb:200002
#: 063b832bffb04c82b9c27f313cf180d8
msgid "Step 3: Extracting and Visualizing Residuals"
msgstr "Step 3: 残差（Residuals）の抽出と可視化"

#: ../../how-to/fitting/advanced_arima.ipynb:200003
#: 307962765b6b4da6acda50fba30c8d22
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"By subtracting the \"stationary noise\" predicted by the model, we obtain "
"the residuals $x_r = x - \\hat{x}$. This is the whitened data."
msgstr "モデルが予測した「定常ノイズ」を引くことで、残差 $x_r = x - \\hat{x}$ を求めます。これが白色化されたデータとなります。"

#: ../../how-to/fitting/advanced_arima.ipynb:220002
#: e6a78b3a01ac4ab6a97e882fd6203bc6
msgid "Step 4: Evaluation in the Frequency Domain"
msgstr "Step 4: 周波数領域での評価"

#: ../../how-to/fitting/advanced_arima.ipynb:220003
#: 0b2e1d7b1fea453cba1425b281b8f972
msgid "We calculate and compare the Power Spectral Density (PSD)."
msgstr "パワースペクトル密度 (PSD) を計算して比較します。"

#: ../../how-to/fitting/advanced_arima.ipynb:240002
#: 27e78992a85340fba262e6858608990e
msgid "Summary"
msgstr "まとめ"

#: ../../how-to/fitting/advanced_arima.ipynb:240003
#: 4326aeb9a0214233a4720ffd629cb040
msgid ""
"Using `model.residuals()`, whitening can be easily performed without writing"
" complex mathematical formulas."
msgstr "`model.residuals()` を用いることで、複雑な数式を書かずに簡単に白色化処理が実行できます。"

#: ../../how-to/fitting/advanced_arima.ipynb:240004
#: 9bf20df869a441b2ba822748b2fb6dc5
msgid ""
"This technique is very powerful for searching for burst signals in "
"gravitational wave analysis and for extracting ringdown waveforms "
"(exponentially decaying sinusoids) immediately after events."
msgstr "この手法は、重力波解析におけるバースト信号の探索や、イベント直後のリングダウン波形（指数減衰する正弦波）の抽出に非常に強力です。"
